{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Synergistic AMPs, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (45.83%) to Uperin 2.7 K: 28%, I=G: 17%, L=A: 11%. GRAVY: -0.061; Mol Wt: 1898.371; mol formula: C85H157N23O22S1; mol ex coeff: 0. Activity: active against Gram- S. typhimurium CGMCC1.1174 (MIC 12.5 uM), E. coli CCTCC AB 2012883 and 10 clinical strains (MIC 6.25-50 uM), P. aeruginosa 4 clinical strains (MIC 50->50), A. baumannii 6 clinical strains (MIC 25-100 uM), S. dysenteriae CGMCC 1.1869 (MIC 50 uM), P-vulgaris CGMCC 1.1651 (MIC >50 uM), Gram+ E. faecium 2 clinical strains (MIC 50-100 uM), S. albus CGMCC 1.3374 (MIC 12.5 uM), S.aureus 4 clincial strains (MIC>100 uM), and S. citreus CCTCC AB 91115 (MIC 6.25 uM). Inhibit the formation of biofilms:bacteria:E. coli. Synergy:antibiotics:Doxycycline: Synergy with Doxycycline against E. coli and synergy with Synergy:antibiotics:Azithromycin or Synergy:antibiotics:Erythromycin against S. albus.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "36432731", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Pharmaceutics. 2022 Nov 21;14(11):2540. doi: 10.3390/pharmaceutics14112540. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04654", "source_id": "AP04654", "source_numeric_id": "04654", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04654", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Antibacterial Potential Analysis of Novel alpha-Helix Peptides in the Chinese Wolf Spider Lycosa sinensis.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Synergistic AMPs, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (52.63%) to LC-AMP-F1 K: 26%, G: 16%, L: 21%. GRAVY: 0.216; Mol Wt: 2048.591; mol formula: C95H170N24O23S1; mol ex coeff: 1490. Activity: active against Gram- S. typhimurium CGMCC1.1174 (MIC 12.5 uM), E. coli CCTCC AB 2012883 and 10 clinical strains (MIC 12.5-50 uM), P. aeruginosa 4 clinical strains (MIC 25->50), A. baumannii 6 clinical strains (MIC 3.1-25 uM), S. dysenteriae CGMCC 1.1869 (MIC 25 uM), P-vulgaris CGMCC 1.1651 (MIC >50 uM), Gram+ E. faecium 2 clinical strains (MIC 12.5 uM), S. albus CGMCC 1.3374 (MIC 6.25 uM), S. aureus 4 clincial strains (MIC 25-100 uM), and S. citreus CCTCC AB 91115 (MIC 6.25 uM). Antibiofilm:bacteria: Inhibited bacterial biofilm formation:E. coli. Synergy:antibiotics:Azithromycin: Synergy with Azithromycin, Synergy:antibiotics:Erythromycin, and Synergy:antibiotics:Doxycycline against E. coli or S. albus.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "36432731", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Pharmaceutics. 2022 Nov 21;14(11):2540. doi: 10.3390/pharmaceutics14112540. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04655", "source_id": "AP04655", "source_numeric_id": "04655", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04655", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Antibacterial Potential Analysis of Novel alpha-Helix Peptides in the Chinese Wolf Spider Lycosa sinensis.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
